8815: \subsection{Command-run boundary}
8816: 
8817: \begin{proposition}[Command-run boundary inventory]
8818: \label{audit:command-run-boundary-inventory}
8819: For the current presentation package, Table~\ref{tab:command-boundary-inventory}
8820: is complete for the command-boundary claims used by
8821: Proposition~\ref{prop:machine-readable-certificate-records},
8822: Proposition~\ref{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition},
8823: Theorem~\ref{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary},
8824: Theorem~\ref{thm:post-inventory-package-fixed-point}, and the finite-record
8825: interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  The accepted
8826: command-boundary claims in the package are exactly the three refreshed finite record-verifier invocations recorded in
8827: \path{review_bundle/certificate_verification_run.log},
8828: \path{review_bundle/source_interface_verification_run.log}, and
8829: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory_freshness_2026-06-09.log}, the
8830: refreshed theorem-environment extractor invocation recorded in
8831: \path{review_bundle/theorem_environment_extraction_run.log}, the byte-level final
8832: digest generation recorded in \path{review_bundle/final_digest_generation_run.log},
8833: together with the dated live venue and bibliography freshness check recorded in
8834: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log}.  The
8835: Lean/BEDC source theorem semantics, publication-daemon or route-state surfaces,
8836: and Rule110/\allowbreak GroundCompiler artifact surfaces remain path-verified,
8837: historical, or bounded-artifact evidence and are not command-run validation
8838: claims.
